    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is headlined by **Bryson Stott** (72.46) and **Daulton Varsho** (65.35), our two strongest starts. **Bryson Stott** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against V\u00e1squez, whose 4.75 xERA combined with a +13% platoon edge makes him our most efficient play. **Daulton Varsho** earns his high ranking through a combination of lineup positioning and a strategic bonus for facing a slow-delivery pitcher, which maximizes his potential to secure a critical stolen base\u2014our scarcest category. Meanwhile, **Gleyber Torres** (60.60) is the final player to clear the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, leveraging a lead-off spot against Matz to provide a steady floor for our Roto categories.\n\nOur most difficult decision occurred at the fringe of the bench, where **Masyn Winn** (39.49) fell just short of the 40-point efficiency floor. While **Masyn Winn** offers value, facing Eovaldi\u2014an elite arm with a 3.29 xERA\u2014crushed his projection, leading to his exclusion to preserve our game caps. Elsewhere, **Jonathan Aranda** (57.71) and **Taylor Ward** (57.10) remain active despite sub-60 scores, as their projected production remains superior to our remaining reserves, such as **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Tyler Freeman**, or **Dylan Beavers**, who are either currently out of the lineup or lack favorable platoon environments today.\n\nWe must monitor **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman** closely; both are facing Harrison (3.41 xERA), resulting in scores barely hovering above the 40-point threshold. Their projections are heavily dampened by the \"SP Skill\" penalty, which accounts for Harrison\u2019s ability to limit production. Furthermore, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (56.07) warrants caution; despite being an elite hitter, the combination of a tough matchup against Schlittler and a negative platoon split creates a lower-than-usual ceiling. We continue to track the health of **Cal Raleigh** and **Will Smith** while hoping **Lawrence Butler**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Drew Gilbert** find their way back into their respective daily rotations to improve our overall depth.",
